WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.020 --> 01:39.800
Episode 18:
A Mother and Child's Close Encounter

01:57.240 --> 01:59.450
Wow... It's beautiful.

02:04.410 --> 02:06.640
Remy is somewhere in this town.

02:10.000 --> 02:13.240
Remy, do you remember us?

02:16.840 --> 02:19.320
I made a promise to Mr. Vitalis

02:19.340 --> 02:22.570
that I would accept you as a daughter of the Milligan family.

02:22.590 --> 02:24.430
You'll stay here, won't you, Remy?

02:24.610 --> 02:26.620
You'll be with us, won't you?

02:27.220 --> 02:33.050
Oh Arthur, I like you and Mrs. Milligan so much.

02:33.430 --> 02:38.390
I want to stay here, too. I don't want to separate from you.

02:39.270 --> 02:43.460
It's Mr. Vitalis' wish that you live here.

02:43.480 --> 02:44.890
Stay here, Remy.

02:45.660 --> 02:50.890
But... I have to go, otherwise Mr. Vitalis will be all alone.

02:55.480 --> 02:57.150
Thank you very much.

02:57.730 --> 03:00.900
I'll never forget you.

03:01.380 --> 03:02.910
Remy...

03:04.450 --> 03:07.880
Arthur, take care of your mother.

03:09.200 --> 03:10.590
Goodbye!

03:10.600 --> 03:14.800
Remy... Remy! Remy!

03:15.980 --> 03:19.560
It's great that Remy's my real sister.

03:19.570 --> 03:21.090
Master...
- Ah...

03:21.720 --> 03:23.730
You are out here again...

03:23.760 --> 03:28.090
You will catch a cold. It's still cold in the morning.

03:28.820 --> 03:32.650
Arthur, you were supposed to be resting.

03:32.670 --> 03:35.850
It's because I was thinking about Remy.

03:35.860 --> 03:39.140
Hasn't Remy been found yet? I want to see her soon.

03:39.150 --> 03:44.470
Master, the Madam has been doing all she can.

03:44.510 --> 03:48.150
Today, the lawyer, Mr. Blair, will visit us, won't he?

03:48.160 --> 03:48.620
Yes...

03:49.420 --> 03:52.140
I hope he brings good news.

03:52.370 --> 03:54.970
Mother, Remy will be found, right?

03:55.000 --> 03:56.260
For sure... Right?

03:56.720 --> 03:58.130
Arthur...

04:01.480 --> 04:03.300
She will be found for sure.

04:03.320 --> 04:05.260
Yes, we will surely find her.

04:09.210 --> 04:14.830
<i>God, please protect Remy, our Remy...</i>

04:19.190 --> 04:22.300
Come on, let's go.

04:24.330 --> 04:27.000
Remy! Remy!
- Hurry and wake up.

04:27.070 --> 04:28.360
I'm getting up now.

04:30.370 --> 04:31.920
Good morning.

04:32.010 --> 04:34.490
Everyone's left already.
- Huh?

04:35.910 --> 04:37.540
It's time already?

04:41.730 --> 04:43.960
I was having such a great dream.

04:46.180 --> 04:46.850
A dream?

04:47.090 --> 04:52.050
Yeah. In the dream, a lady was calling me in a sweet voice.

04:52.080 --> 04:52.680
You guys!

04:53.920 --> 04:55.640
What's taking so long?

04:55.990 --> 04:58.640
You're gonna be late. Get going!

05:02.390 --> 05:04.650
I'll go to the same place as usual.

05:05.130 --> 05:08.160
And I'll go the market place.
- Oh, yes.

05:08.800 --> 05:11.420
Please watch out for the kids on St. Michel Boulevard.

05:11.530 --> 05:15.570
Yesterday, Jack's money was almost stolen.

05:16.120 --> 05:19.080
Albert got his money stolen just a while ago.

05:19.490 --> 05:22.200
The kids there are so rude.

05:22.290 --> 05:24.470
We should walk home together.

05:24.490 --> 05:26.540
Let's meet here in the evening.

05:26.610 --> 05:28.750
Yeah, see you later.

05:32.380 --> 05:36.730
Sir, have you found Remy yet?

05:36.860 --> 05:39.220
Unfortunately not.

05:39.700 --> 05:41.710
I've been looking for her all over the place.

05:42.130 --> 05:46.240
But I haven't even figured out how many traveling performers

05:46.760 --> 05:51.240
in Paris have a little girl and animals.

05:51.870 --> 05:53.460
I see.

05:53.740 --> 05:56.780
That man, Mr. Vitalis, told you that he would be going to Paris, right?

05:57.050 --> 06:01.630
Yes, he told me that he would perform in Paris during the winter.

06:01.720 --> 06:02.580
Hmmmm...

06:04.390 --> 06:07.690
Could you show me the cameo used as evidence?

06:07.690 --> 06:08.320
Yes.

06:08.530 --> 06:10.800
Madam, I'll get it.

06:10.830 --> 06:12.010
Yes, please do.

06:18.490 --> 06:21.010
Arthur, you'll get sick if you stay out here.

06:21.070 --> 06:23.020
Please, go back to your room.

06:23.190 --> 06:28.960
Please mother, let me stay here. I really want to know about Remy.

06:30.330 --> 06:32.710
Fine.
- Great.

06:32.840 --> 06:36.030
Please give it to him, Mary.
- Yes, Madam.

06:37.600 --> 06:39.850
Here it is.
- Let's take a look.

06:41.620 --> 06:43.260
Beautiful cameo, isn’t it?

06:43.750 --> 06:49.020
When Remy was born, this is what my husband gave me and Remy.

06:49.260 --> 06:53.320
I saw Remy carrying the same thing.

06:54.640 --> 06:58.000
Arthur! Arthur!

06:58.260 --> 07:01.370
Mary, please take care of Arthur.
- Yes, Madam.

07:07.800 --> 07:13.280
I let her go without even knowing she was my daughter.

07:13.620 --> 07:16.560
Somewhere in that city, Remy's...

07:21.510 --> 07:22.550
Sir?

07:23.050 --> 07:23.780
Yes?

07:23.960 --> 07:28.170
Please, find Remy as soon as possible.

07:28.200 --> 07:31.030
Certainly, I will do my best.

07:32.040 --> 07:33.550
Madam,

07:33.870 --> 07:36.320
your son has fallen asleep.

07:36.320 --> 07:37.770
Thank you, Mary.

07:38.310 --> 07:42.050
It seems the Paris climate doesn't agree with him.

07:42.340 --> 07:44.990
He's had a bad cough these days.

07:45.540 --> 07:49.060
Mary, please go and get the prescribed medicine.

07:49.110 --> 07:50.280
Yes, Madam.

08:13.620 --> 08:17.420
The lady in my dream looked like my mother.

08:17.960 --> 08:20.740
She called me Remy in a sweet voice.

08:24.130 --> 08:25.300
Mother...

08:26.950 --> 08:29.920
I wonder if I can meet my real mother some day.

08:31.590 --> 08:34.120
I do hope I find her.
- Remy!

08:37.810 --> 08:39.100
Did you sell all your flowers?

08:39.470 --> 08:42.070
Here! Look! Today’s sales were really good.

08:42.070 --> 08:44.040
I see. That's great.

08:44.540 --> 08:46.200
Were you looking at the cameo again?

08:46.420 --> 08:49.370
Yes, it's my treasure.

08:49.570 --> 08:50.710
It's beautiful.

08:51.110 --> 08:54.220
Hey, that's really nice.

08:58.010 --> 09:00.130
It's very valuable.

09:00.190 --> 09:03.440
Yeah, we could sell it to a jewelry store.

09:05.220 --> 09:07.750
Give it to me.
- No.

09:07.990 --> 09:09.070
Give it to me!

09:09.630 --> 09:11.430
Ah! Give it back!

09:11.500 --> 09:12.180
Here!

09:14.250 --> 09:14.940
Let's go.

09:15.820 --> 09:16.680
Wait!

09:20.050 --> 09:23.070
Give us all the money you have with you.

09:26.710 --> 09:28.450
What's with this dog?

09:32.090 --> 09:36.390
Shit, that's enough for today.

09:38.570 --> 09:41.760
Wait!
- Remy, don't! They're dangerous!

09:57.460 --> 09:59.530
Big brother Mattia!

10:00.210 --> 10:01.710
Mattia!

10:06.890 --> 10:09.710
There's trouble! The kids on St. Michel Boulevard...

10:09.720 --> 10:10.920
Did you get beaten up by them?

10:11.120 --> 10:13.660
We're all right, but Remy...

10:15.640 --> 10:18.510
Traveling entertainers with a dog and monkey?

10:18.540 --> 10:19.090
Yes.

10:19.610 --> 10:24.500
An old man and a little girl. Have you seen them?

10:24.550 --> 10:26.180
Well...

10:27.630 --> 10:30.120
I don't know.

10:30.560 --> 10:31.600
I see.

10:32.370 --> 10:33.910
Thank you very much.

10:38.120 --> 10:40.530
Hey, be careful!

10:41.610 --> 10:43.390
Wait!

11:32.460 --> 11:34.420
I wonder where they've gone.

11:36.140 --> 11:37.350
Shit.

11:44.930 --> 11:47.970
You sure have guts to follow us here.

11:48.440 --> 11:50.220
Give me back my pendant!

11:51.060 --> 11:51.590
Heh.

12:25.730 --> 12:28.110
Give it back to me!
That's my pendant!

12:28.900 --> 12:30.690
You're a brash girl!

12:35.010 --> 12:36.980
If you want it so badly, then take it back.

12:38.870 --> 12:40.940
Here, don't you want this?

12:41.380 --> 12:43.960
Give it back! Give it back!

12:43.980 --> 12:44.770
Got it!

12:45.220 --> 12:46.360
Nuh-uh! Here!

12:48.060 --> 12:48.680
Here!

12:52.820 --> 12:53.830
Catch!

12:55.490 --> 12:57.510
What's wrong? Are you scared?

13:11.290 --> 13:16.600
You! You really want to get beat up don't you?

13:19.750 --> 13:22.090
You stupid...
- Stop it!

13:23.440 --> 13:24.540
Get your hands off of Remy!

13:24.780 --> 13:25.950
Mattia!

13:26.850 --> 13:27.780
You...

13:28.330 --> 13:31.280
It's embarrassing to fight against a girl.

13:31.410 --> 13:33.160
I'll fight with you.

13:33.510 --> 13:34.590
Come on, Paul.

13:34.790 --> 13:36.220
A man-to-man fight.

13:36.330 --> 13:38.290
Huh, you cheeky little...

13:38.300 --> 13:41.180
I've been waiting to knock you out one day.

13:41.310 --> 13:42.170
All right.

13:42.200 --> 13:43.100
Come on!

13:43.430 --> 13:44.790
Do your worst!

13:52.750 --> 13:56.520
Now, big brother Mattia!
Hit him! Go on!

14:00.090 --> 14:01.280
Crap!

14:01.410 --> 14:05.910
Come on Paul!
- Go on! Knock him out!

14:12.920 --> 14:13.890
The final blow!

14:20.240 --> 14:21.890
Guys, knock him out!

14:21.890 --> 14:24.290
That's not fair! This is our fight!

14:24.560 --> 14:27.000
Huh! We don't care if it's fair or unfair.

14:27.890 --> 14:28.970
Crap!

14:28.970 --> 14:29.740
Mattia!

14:36.130 --> 14:36.860
Oh...

14:38.510 --> 14:40.050
Okay, run!

14:49.290 --> 14:52.330
After them!
Don't let them get away!

14:53.300 --> 14:55.790
Take care.
- Thank you.

15:06.610 --> 15:07.720
They're coming.

15:08.880 --> 15:09.850
This way!

15:11.570 --> 15:12.700
Go straight!

15:17.390 --> 15:19.060
Take this!

15:24.710 --> 15:27.770
Maria, Lise, hurry up!
- Lise, this way!

15:28.700 --> 15:31.240
Capi, protect them!

15:31.720 --> 15:33.000
Remy!

15:33.830 --> 15:35.620
What are you doing here?

15:35.710 --> 15:36.830
Hurry and run.

15:36.830 --> 15:40.560
But my pendant...

15:42.120 --> 15:43.950
Shit, they are pesky.

15:44.000 --> 15:44.790
Come on.

15:56.160 --> 15:57.660
Remy, this way!

16:02.580 --> 16:05.200
Hey, go look for them!
Make sure you find them!

16:05.860 --> 16:07.290
You guys look around over there.

16:07.290 --> 16:08.150
Okay!

16:15.560 --> 16:18.090
No... I can't run anymore.

16:19.060 --> 16:21.090
Come on! Do you want to get caught?

16:21.090 --> 16:23.050
But...
- Did you find them?

16:23.140 --> 16:24.820
No, they're not here.

16:25.410 --> 16:26.950
Where have they gone?

16:31.340 --> 16:33.590
The coughing's finally stopped.

16:33.660 --> 16:37.090
It looked painful, so I was worried.

16:37.760 --> 16:41.570
The air in Paris isn't good for his health.

16:42.010 --> 16:45.650
I think it's better to go back to Toulouse as soon as possible.

16:45.650 --> 16:49.350
Remy... Remy...

16:57.110 --> 16:58.940
Mary, I've made up my mind.

16:59.490 --> 17:02.680
I can't let Arthur stay here anymore.

17:03.410 --> 17:05.700
Then I will go to Toulouse.

17:05.700 --> 17:09.630
No... I will take Arthur there.

17:09.890 --> 17:11.150
Then, what about Remy?

17:12.470 --> 17:15.130
I have a favor to ask you.

17:16.040 --> 17:16.880
Yes, Madam.

17:17.580 --> 17:20.140
I'd like you to stay here and find Remy.

17:20.630 --> 17:21.570
Madam.

17:21.570 --> 17:26.670
Mary, in this big city of Paris, you're the only one who knows Remy’s face.

17:32.950 --> 17:34.400
Will you do it?

17:36.630 --> 17:43.110
I will do it, Madam.
I will surely find Remy.

17:43.790 --> 17:46.750
I'm counting on you. I'm looking forward to good news.

17:46.810 --> 17:48.180
Yes, Madam.

18:02.530 --> 18:05.480
Mattia, what do we do?
- There they are!

18:05.610 --> 18:06.960
Stop!

18:06.960 --> 18:09.820
I'll teach you to mess with me!

18:10.000 --> 18:10.820
Mattia!

18:10.860 --> 18:13.220
Ah... Remy, give me a hand.

18:14.340 --> 18:16.350
Downstairs! Let's go!

18:21.480 --> 18:22.190
Come on!

18:24.700 --> 18:25.340
Hurry up!

18:33.610 --> 18:35.200
Remy, they're coming!

18:37.350 --> 18:38.430
Hurry up!

18:40.770 --> 18:41.520
Ah...

18:43.550 --> 18:45.490
Sorry about that, Paul.

18:45.490 --> 18:48.690
If you won't give up then come over here.

18:49.670 --> 18:51.860
Crap. I won't let you go!

19:02.190 --> 19:03.830
Are you all right, Remy?

19:03.890 --> 19:07.290
Yes, are they still chasing us?

19:07.510 --> 19:10.440
They're tough. This way.

19:14.050 --> 19:17.540
I don't see them.
Where are they?

19:17.540 --> 19:20.950
Shit. They're quick on their feet.

19:20.950 --> 19:23.770
Where have they gone?
- Over there, I guess.

19:23.840 --> 19:27.100
Right. Let's look around in town one more time.

19:27.150 --> 19:27.810
Yeah.

19:35.010 --> 19:36.420
It's safe now.

19:37.860 --> 19:39.050
They're gone, aren't they?

19:42.930 --> 19:44.070
Let's go home.

19:48.550 --> 19:49.520
What's wrong?

19:50.600 --> 19:53.040
My pendant was stolen.

20:01.290 --> 20:02.100
Here.

20:06.140 --> 20:09.220
Wow... You got it back?

20:10.150 --> 20:12.520
Thank goodness.

20:15.950 --> 20:19.940
This was given to me by my real mother.

20:20.160 --> 20:22.450
It's my precious treasure.

20:22.590 --> 20:26.280
I feel like I'll be able to meet my mother someday if I keep it with me.

20:28.690 --> 20:30.520
You're lucky that you know your mother's out there.

20:30.870 --> 20:31.660
Huh?

20:32.760 --> 20:38.030
My dad and mom died when I was Lise's age.

20:38.240 --> 20:41.870
I was taken to an orphanage and later sent to a circus.

20:42.060 --> 20:44.860
Then the leader sold me to Gaspard.

20:51.900 --> 20:53.320
Take care of it.

20:53.950 --> 20:54.920
Yup.

21:13.850 --> 21:16.540
Remy, just be patient.

21:17.510 --> 21:20.790
We will be able to see you soon. I think.

21:25.200 --> 21:26.370
Mattia...

21:28.860 --> 21:29.760
Thank you.

21:31.550 --> 21:35.030
I thought that you hated me.

21:37.350 --> 21:38.910
I don't hate you.

21:39.220 --> 21:41.670
Huh? Did you say something?

21:41.930 --> 21:43.830
It was nothing.

21:44.180 --> 21:45.320
Wait!

21:47.070 --> 21:49.510
Mattia, wait!

21:55.920 --> 22:04.500
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:05.570 --> 22:16.400
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:16.910 --> 22:26.810
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:26.920 --> 22:36.640
From the future that gives us our fate

22:36.770 --> 22:45.480
Try to seek for them more

22:46.360 --> 22:50.130
Give your heart to

22:50.260 --> 23:05.250
That person who is also seeking you

23:18.060 --> 23:21.370
Wow...
It looks just like Mr. Vitalis' horse cart.

23:21.650 --> 23:23.170
I feel nostalgic.

23:23.220 --> 23:26.460
Oh... What a wonderful dog.
- Are you a street performer, too?

23:26.890 --> 23:27.960
Yes.

23:28.210 --> 23:30.430
I'm Remy. What's your name?

23:33.100 --> 23:36.560
<i>A Traveling Family</i>

23:33.100 --> 23:36.560
Next time:
